

 tital-Airport Network Using Dijkstra’s Algorithm

1.Problem statement
Develop an airport network using a graph in which airports are represented as vertices and flight travel times are represented as edges with non-negative weights. Apply Dijkstra’s algorithm to find the minimum-travel-time paths from a selected airport to all other reachable airports.

2. Objective

1.To represent an airport network using a graph.
2.To assign non-negative travel-time weights between airports.
3.To implement Dijkstra’s algorithm.
4.To find the shortest travel time from a source airport to other airports.

3. Algorithm

1.Start the program.
2.Create a graph of airports with travel-time weights.
3.Select Mumbai as the source airport.
4.Initialize its distance to zero and all other distances to infinity.
5.Select the airport with the minimum temporary distance.
6.Update the distances of its connected airports if a shorter path is found.
7.Repeat until the priority queue becomes empty.
8.Display the minimum travel time to each airport.
9.Stop.

4.Result

The airport network was successfully represented using a weighted graph. Dijkstra’s algorithm was implemented to calculate the minimum travel time from Mumbai to all reachable airports.

5.Conclusion

Dijkstra’s algorithm efficiently finds the shortest paths in an airport network when all travel-time weights are non-negative. It helps determine the minimum total travel time between airports.